# The World — the canon

> **SETUP AGENT: this is a synthesis template.** Write the live file to
> `content/world.md`; delete every guidance blockquote. **The learner approves the cast
> before anything uses it.** Keep the section headings and the cast-table shape exactly:
> `scripts/world.py` parses them (a name in bold, its target-language form in
> parentheses, the pinned voice in backticks as the last cell; `## 4. This arc`;
> `### Beat log` with `*(empty)*`). Worked example: `docs/WORKED_EXAMPLE.md` → The world.

**Fictional. Always.** Nobody here is anyone the learner knows, and no name, role or
situation is lifted from their real life. A parallel world can be funny, awkward and wrong
about things, which a portrait of real people cannot.

**Who writes what.** Setup drafts Place, Cast and Standing facts; **the learner approves the
cast before anything consumes it.** After that the tutor writes the arc premise at the
month cut, and each rendered episode appends one beat line. The learner overrides anything.

**Budget: 1,200 words.** Canon that outgrows it is compressed at the month boundary — the
arc's beat log collapses to one past-arc line. The number is never raised to fit more lore.

